title: 'Paradigm-Atelier symbiosis: detection + 4-augmentation contract'
summary: 'Implemented the symbiosis protocol agreed with the owner: when atelier studio --new runs in a Paradigm-initialized directory, four idempotent augmentations weave Atelier into the existing Paradigm scaffold without overwriting anything Paradigm owns. (1) CLAUDE.md gets a sentinel-bracketed Atelier section appended/replaced. (2) .claude/agents/ gets the three atelier-quill/lux/iris.md agent files dropped (canonical sync from embedded templates in atelier-agent-templates.ts). (3) .mcp.json gets the atelier server merged alongside paradigm (preserves permissions block + other servers). (4) .paradigm/personas/index.yaml gets the three atelier persona entries added via YAML merge. New --no-paradigm-integration escape hatch on atelier studio --new. Detection-and-augmentation model keeps Paradigm and Atelier codebases decoupled — no Paradigm-side preset registration needed.'
