  - packages/cli/src/index.test.ts
  - packages/cli/.purpose
learnings:
  - Detection-and-augmentation in the consumer (atelier) beats preset registration in the producer (paradigm) when two tools need to cooperate without coupling. The augmentation logic lives where the consumer can evolve it independently of the producer's release cadence.
  - Sentinel-bracketed markdown sections make CLAUDE.md augmentation safely idempotent across re-runs. Same pattern would work for any owned-by-another-tool config file we need to extend.
